[executive]
# ============================================================================
# O_o_Reader validation deck: solid stresses in their material systems (PSOLID CORDM) (SOL 101)
#
# Validates:
#   - the stresses and strains of identical CHEXA and CTETRA blocks under the
#     same load, written in the basic system (CORDM 0), the element system
#     (CORDM -1), a turned rectangular system, a cylindrical and a spherical
#     system: the system word of each entry and the values in each system (the
#     CORDM 0 block is the reference)
# Settles (library item: current status):
#   - solidStress and solidStrain to element and material systems
#     (refused: no file shows a solid result stored in its element system, a
#     rule of the format reference); a solid with a cylindrical
#     or spherical CORDM or CORDM below 0 (refused: where the curvilinear
#     system is evaluated is not in the format reference)
# Written for this project, to exercise the reader.
# How to run it, what to bring back: validation/models/README.md.
# ============================================================================
SolutionSequence;101
[case]
TitleText;O_o_Reader validation: solid stresses in material systems
BulkEcho;Sorted
SinglePointConstrSelection;1
StaticLoadSelection;1
DisplacementOutput;All;PlotOnly
StressOutput;All;PlotOnly;PrintListing;CornerResults
StrainOutput;All;PlotOnly;PrintListing;CornerResults
SubcaseStart;1
LabelText;the same tip load on every block
[model]
# Output files: OUTPUT2 (PARAM,POST,-1) and the HDF5 database (double precision,
# deflate).
Parameter;PostprocessingFile;-1
ResultFileParams;Precision;64;CompressionMethod;GzipCompression
# Five identical CHEXA cantilever blocks (10 x 10 x 30, clamped at x = 0, the
# same tip load), one for each material system of their PSOLID: CORDM 0
# (basic), -1 (element system), 5 (a rectangular system turned about x, y and
# z), 6 (a cylindrical system whose axis is the block's axis), 8 (a spherical
# system); and the same five as CTETRA blocks (5 tetrahedra a cube). Units:
# mm, N, tonne.
IsoMat;1;7.E+4;;0.33;2.7E-9
RectFrame2;5;;0.;0.;0.;0.3;0.4;1.;1.;0.2;0.1
CylindricalFrame2;6;;0.;5.;5.;1.;5.;5.;0.;6.;5.
SphericalFrame2;8;;-10.;5.;5.;-10.;5.;6.;-9.;5.;5.
SolidProp;10;1;0
SolidProp;11;1;-1
SolidProp;12;1;5
SolidProp;13;1;6
SolidProp;14;1;8
